<title>EGYPT: Egypt yr/yr money supply up 12.9 pct in Jan 97.</title>
<headline>Egypt yr/yr money supply up 12.9 pct in Jan 97.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 12.9 percent in the year ending January 1997, from 12.2 percent in the year to December 1996, the Central Bank of Egypt said in a bulletin.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 180.089 billion pounds at end-January 1997 against 178.598 billion at end-December.</p>
<p>Following figures, all in billions, were supplied by the Central Bank.</p>
<p>					  Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>    Total money supply	   180.089   178.598   159.551</p>
<p>    Money			     38.018    37.099    33.552</p>
<p>    Quasi-money		    142.071   141.499   125.999</p>
<p>    Year-on-year growth (pct)   +12.9     +12.2	 --</p>
<p>    Month-on-month growth (pct) +0.83     +1.17     +0.27</p>
<p>The Central Bank figures differ slightly from those published by the International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
